  "final_response": "To create a lightweight tag, run the `git tag` command with only the tag name—omit `-a`, `-s`, and `-m` options:\n\n```bash\ngit tag v1.4-lw\n```\n\nA lightweight tag is just a reference that stores only the commit’s SHA‑1 checksum (the commit checksum) and no additional metadata such as tagger, date, or message; it never moves and always points to the same commit. [tagging.005-lightweight-tags]",
